    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b2d6604864094a4dee1479308460aace275a3719cb7a06ae390bda4600c9f291",
      "text": "After breakfast, you will head to Quilotoa crater lake. The day takes about 10 hours, including travel. The drive to Quilotoa takes around 2 hours, and the journey from Quilotoa to Baños takes about 3.5 hours. The tour reaches 3,900 m, where temperatures are around +10 °C.\n\nThe route heads towards the Central Andes and then follows the road known as the Pujilí Route. At Quilotoa, you will go up to a viewpoint overlooking the crater lake and have a chance to walk through an Indigenous community.\n\nIf everyone in the group wants to, you can walk down to the water, go kayaking and ride mules back up. Kayak hire and mule rides cost extra. Local residents offer the mule rides informally, and they are usually available until around 15:00.\n\nAfter Quilotoa, you will continue to Baños. The road descends gradually from the cold highlands to the milder valley near Tungurahua Volcano.\n\n**Accommodation:** Samari 5*.  \n**Meals:** breakfast.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6krd1q-6gkvrjmldy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
